The 2024–25 season was the 97th season in the history of CD Leganés and the first in the top flight since 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.flashscore.com/news/soccer-laliga2-leganes-win-spanish-second-division-to-return-to-laliga-after-four-years/YJlJwoi2/|title=Leganes win Spanish second division to return to LaLiga after four years &#124; Flashscore.com|website=www.flashscore.com}}</ref> In addition to the domestic league, the team participated in the [[Copa del Rey]].

== Summary ==
On 14 June, as a result of gaining promotion, the purchase clause was activated for midfielder [[Darko Brašanac]], who was loaned from Osasuna to continue for one year with the Madrid region club.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://as.com/futbol/segunda/oficial-el-leganes-compra-a-brasanac-por-solo-una-temporada-n/|title=Oficial: El Leganés compra a Brasanac por sólo una temporada|first=Kiko|last=Martín|date=June 14, 2024|website=Diario AS}}</ref>

